'''Szombathelyi Haladás''' is a [[Hungary|Hungarian]] [[football (soccer)|football]] club based in [[Szombathely]]. ''Haladás'' is the [[Hungarian language|Hungarian]] word for ''progress''. The club, which was founded in 1919, plays its home games at [[Rohonci úti Stadion]] which has a capacity of 12,000 (4,000 seats). The club colours are green and white.

Haladás reached the [[Hungarian Cup]] final in the years 1975, 1993 and 2002. Since its first promotion in 1936 the club has spent 51 seasons in the first division of the Hungarian league, the [[Hungarian National Championship I|Nemzeti Bajnokság I (NB I)]].

After the 2006/07 season, the club missed out on promotion to the NB I because of an 11 points deduction for the use of ineligible players. [[BFC Siófok]] was promoted in the place of Haladás.

Season 2007/08 Haladás won the second division, and started the next season in the highest level in Hungary again.

In the 2008/09 season Haladás reached the best rank ever in the history of the team: "Hali" won the bronze medal, and got the right to start the qualification rounds in the [[Europa League]].

