'''Dagenham & Redbridge Football Club''' ({{pron-en|ˈdægənəm ˈrɛdˌbrɪdʒ}}) is an [[England|English]] [[football (soccer)|football]] team based in [[Dagenham]], in the [[London Borough of Barking & Dagenham]], [[London, England]]. It was formed in 1992 after a merger between [[Redbridge Forest F.C.|Redbridge Forest]] and [[Dagenham F.C.|Dagenham]]. The team currently plays in [[Football League Two]] having been promoted as champions from the [[Football Conference]] in the [[2006-07 in English football|2006&ndash;07]] season.

The club's traditional colours are red and blue, to represent the merger teams colours. In the early days the club used red for the home shirt and blue for the away shirts, normally red and white vertical stripes for the home and blue and white vertical stripes for the away. In recent times the kit has gone under a large transformation. The stripes have been replaced with solid colours. The away colours are now yellow with blue trim.

==History==
{{Unreferenced section|date=November 2008}}
===Formation===
The club can trace its origins back to four amateur clubs '''[[Ilford F.C.|Ilford]]''' (formed in [[1881 in football (soccer)|1881]]), '''[[Leytonstone F.C.|Leytonstone]]''' (1886), '''[[Walthamstow Avenue F.C.|Walthamstow Avenue]]''' ([[1900 in football (soccer)|1900]]) and '''[[Dagenham F.C.|Dagenham]]''' (1949). All had some success, particularly Leytonstone, who won the [[FA Amateur Cup]] three times and the [[Isthmian League]] title nine times.

In [[1979 in football (soccer)|1979]], Ilford and Leytonstone merged to become '''[[Redbridge Forest F.C.|Leytonstone/Ilford]]''', and in [[1988 in football (soccer)|1988]] they absorbed the struggling Walthamstow Avenue to become '''[[Redbridge Forest F.C.|Redbridge Forest]]''' (although the name change was made only in the summer of 1989). Redbridge Forest achieved promotion to the [[Football Conference]] in [[1991 in football (soccer)|1991]] before merging with Dagenham in [[1992 in football (soccer)|1992]] to become Dagenham & Redbridge.

===Non-league===
Dagenham & Redbridge spent several seasons in the [[Football Conference]], but were relegated to the [[Isthmian League Premier Division]] in [[1996 in football (soccer)|1996]]. It remained in the division until winning promotion in 1999&ndash;2000, going on to establish itself as one of the strongest clubs in the Conference, finishing 3rd, 2nd and 5th in its first three seasons back following promotion. The club was only narrowly beaten to the title by [[Boston United F.C.|Boston United]] in 2002. Boston United was subsequently found guilty of inappropriately making illegal payments to its players in its title-winning season, following which Dagenham & Redbridge unsuccessfully attempted to have itself declared Conference Champions, and hence take Boston's contentious place in [[The Football League]].

The Daggers then declined somewhat, finishing the [[2003-04 in English football|2003&ndash;04]], [[2004-05 in English football|2004&ndash;05]] and [[2005-06 in English football|2005&ndash;06]] seasons in mid-table. On [[February 27]] [[2004]] the club was beaten 9-0 at home by [[Hereford United F.C.|Hereford United]], equalling the record highest winning margin in the Conference.<ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_conf/3489720.stm Dag & Red 0-9 Hereford] - BBC Sport</ref>

===Promotion to the Football League===
The [[2006-07 in English football|2006&ndash;07 season]] saw Dagenham & Redbridge battle it out with [[Oxford United F.C.|Oxford United]] for the top of the league spot. Despite Oxford quickly racing to the top, a collapse in Oxford's form combined with an excellent run for the Daggers saw them overtake Oxford in the league. On [[7 April]], Dagenham & Redbridge beat [[Aldershot Town]] 2-1 to be declared Conference Champions, meaning the club would play in the [[Football League]] for the first time in its history.<ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_conf/6513465.stm Dag & Red 2-1 Aldershot] - BBC Sport</ref><ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/teams/d/dagenham_and_redbridge/6532833.stm Daggers delight at promotion prize] - BBC Sport</ref>

Dagenham & Redbridge played its first ever match in The Football League on [[11 August]] [[2007]], a 1-0 defeat to [[Stockport County F.C.|Stockport County]].<ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_div_3/6931028.stm Stockport 1-0 Dag & Red] - BBC Sport</ref> The club won its first Football League game at home to {{fc|Lincoln City}} on 1 September 2007.<ref>[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_div_3/6963604.stm Dag & Red 1-0 Lincoln] - BBC Sport</ref> The Daggers finished the season in 20th place, ensuring a second season of Football League competition. Promotion to the Football League meant that Dagenham & Redbridge could compete in the [[Football League Cup|League Cup]] for the first time. The club lost in the First Round to [[Luton Town F.C.|Luton Town]].

The [[2008-09 in English football|following season]], the Daggers reached their highest ever position of 8th. They just failed to make the League 2 play offs after losing to [[Shropshire]] side [[Shrewsbury Town F.C.|Shrewsbury Town]] at home on the last day of the season.

